[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124191,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PUVA keratosis is a hyperkeratotic cutaneous lesion developing on sun-protected skin following prolonged psoralen and ultraviolet&nbsp;A (PUVA) treatment.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124192,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8070/0 PUVA keratosis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124193,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EK90.Y &amp; XH8MN8 Other discrete epidermal dysplasias &amp; PUVA keratosis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124194,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124195,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124196,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The development of PUVA keratoses is confined to areas of previous PUVA therapy and typically affects non&ndash;sun-exposed skin of the trunk and thighs.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124197,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with PUVA keratoses present with multiple warty, hyperkeratotic, and scaly papules with a broad base, measuring from a few millimetres to 10&nbsp;mm {8445056}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124198,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The affected individuals are those receiving PUVA treatment for underlying skin conditions (e.g. psoriasis).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124199,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This type of keratosis arises in association with prolonged medical use of PUVA treatment for skin conditions. The effect is dose-dependent {8445056}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124200,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Frequent <em>TP53</em> (57%) and <em>HRAS</em> (44%) mutations of the ultraviolet (UV) radiation signature type point to UV radiation exposure as the main etiological factor in these lesions {14962108}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124201,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124202,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>PUVA keratoses are well demarcated and characterized by acanthosis and overlying hyperkeratosis. A papillomatous growth and focal parakeratosis may be present. Mild keratinocyte dysplasia is noted in approximately 50% of biopsies. An additional finding is the presence of a superficial dermal chronic inflammatory infiltrate {8445056}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124203,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124204,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124205,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a well-circumscribed squamoproliferative lesion with up to mild squamous dysplasia in the setting of prolonged PUVA treatment.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124206,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 124207,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 8,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is an increased risk of the development of non-melanoma skin cancer, particularly squamous cell carcinoma and less often basal cell carcinoma, years after prolonged PUVA treatment in patients with PUVA keratosis {7430462; 22264671; 8445056}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-23T16:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]